hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"178","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of your wives seeks permission to go to the mosque, he should not prevent her."""
"179","It is narrated from Mawla Abi Zahm, may Allah have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, met a woman on the road. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, asked her: ""Where are you going?"" She replied: ""To the mosque."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""You have set out for the mosque and have also applied perfume?"" She said: ""Yes."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""I heard the Noble Prophet ﷺ say: 'Any woman who applies perfume and then leaves her house for the mosque, her prayer and her fast are not accepted until she returns home and performs a ritual bath (ghusl) as for major impurity.'"""
"180","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from coming to the mosques. They should go out wrapped in large cloaks without adornment."""
"181","‘Abbad bin Tamim narrates from his uncle (Sayyiduna ‘Abdullah bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lying on his back in the mosque with one leg placed over the other."
"182","‘Abbad bin Tamim narrates from his uncle (Sayyiduna ‘Abdullah bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lying flat on his back in the mosque with one leg placed over the other."
"183","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed in a cloak and said: ""This has distracted me from prayer. Take it to Abu Jahm (may Allah be pleased with him) and bring an Anbijani cloak in exchange for it."""
"184","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that Abu Juhm bin Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) presented the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with a Syrian cloak which had stripes on it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed in it. When he returned, he said: ""Return this cloak to Abu Juhm (may Allah be pleased with him). I saw these markings during the prayer and it was close to putting me to trial."""
